course: dictionary
lesson: 8267
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can do different jobs and mean different things. Riding is one word, but its meaning depends on the words around it. Ask yourself: is it an action, a thing, or a describing word?
explain: «Always wear a riding helmet when you ride a horse or pony.» Here riding describes the helmet: it is a helmet for riding. Ride, nearby, is the action, and riding is its -ing form. Context tells you which job the word is doing.
explain: «She is riding her scooter» means she is travelling on it right now. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Riding means travelling on a bike, horse or other thing that carries you.
fact: Horse riding, or horseback riding, is the sport or hobby of riding horses.
fact: Riding is the -ing form of the verb ride, as in «She is riding her scooter».
fact: Riding can also describe a thing used for riding, as in riding boots or a riding helmet.
fact: In Canada, a riding is an area that elects one member of parliament.
exercise: «She is riding her scooter.» What does riding mean here? | Cleaning her scooter | *Travelling on her scooter | Buying a new scooter | Stopping at the park
exercise: «Always wear a riding helmet when you ride a horse or pony.» What kind of word is riding here? | *A describing word, showing what kind of helmet | A name for a person | A word for a place | An action word for a horse
exercise: In Canada, what is a riding? | A road for trains | A kind of bicycle | A horse-riding school | *An area that elects one member of parliament
test: «Dad takes me to my riding lessons on Saturdays.» What does riding mean here? | *The sport or hobby of riding horses | A kind of heavy rain | Walking to school | Cooking dinner for the family
test: «Attila led the Huns, horse-riding warriors from the east.» What are the Huns, described as horse-riding? | Children learning at school | Farmers who grew crops | Ships that sailed on the sea | *Warriors who fought on horseback
exam: «In the 1300s news and armies moved at walking or riding pace.» What does riding pace mean? | *The speed of travelling on a horse or other animal | A pace so slow you have to stop for a rest | The speed of a letter sent by post | The speed of a fast racing car
